        <section id="scrum-roles"  class="t-bg-primary">
          
            <h2>Scrum roles</h2>
              <p>Scroll through the slides below to learn more about the roles within a scrum team.</p>

              
              
<div class="gallery-container">
  <div role="group" class="gallery no-js">
    <ul>
        <li role="listitem">
          
    <div class="l-media ">
        
        <h2 class="l-media__title">
          Product Owner
        </h2>

      <div class="l-media__body ">
        <p>The Product Owner manages the Product Backlog and optimises the value of the Product.  They would have direct relationships with the Business Owner and the Stakeholders.  Before the Planning meeting can take place, the Product Owner would need to determine the priority tasks and decide the sprint goal.  The set of tasks that a product owner does is often referred to as product ownership.</p>

      </div>
          <img class="l-media__img" src="~/images/svg/uc/uc_u5_s4_p2_slide1.svg" alt="" width="300" height="300" >  
    </div>
        </li>
        <li role="listitem">
          
    <div class="l-media ">
        
        <h2 class="l-media__title">
          Scrum Master
        </h2>

      <div class="l-media__body ">
        <p>The Scrum Master manages the Scrum Process and remove impediments.  The Scrum Master would predominately manage the Planning meeting taking into consideration priority, capacity, and the wider business expectations.</p>
<p>They would ensure the agile values and principles are followed by clearing obstacles, support team effectiveness, address team dynamics, support good relationships between the team and others, and protect the team from outside interruptions and distractions.</p>

      </div>
          <img class="l-media__img" src="~/images/svg/uc/uc_u5_s4_p2_slide2.svg" alt="" width="300" height="300" >  
    </div>
        </li>
        <li role="listitem">
          
    <div class="l-media ">
        
        <h2 class="l-media__title">
          The Scrum team
        </h2>

      <div class="l-media__body ">
        <p>The Scrum Team (also known as the Scrum Development Team) organises and manages its own work.  They would deliver the agreed product increment inside a sprint. The team would consist of different skillsets and abilities needed to deliver the product which would likely to include programming, designing, testing, content writing, and/or business skills depending on the project.</p>

      </div>
          <img class="l-media__img" src="~/images/svg/uc/uc_u5_s4_p2_slide3.svg" alt="" width="300" height="300" >  
    </div>
        </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>

            
          
        </section>
        
    
     
    
  
     
    
  
  
